 of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-3,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-3,2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106051/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0346056c-cf8e-51bf-92f3-052a0948a6fa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106051"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79164/selection/eb2bfa7d1225003ce3f59917a7890ef7c00c842fe8fe73de0c4307caa0a0f83c" :answer/id #uuid "09f54a8e-bb85-51fa-9ab0-b01121d9fa8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -6,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79164/selection/5cc03d0427c9f14df5e6f76f8c81e2e8b9376118db124396683cdf59421c7275" :answer/id #uuid "9f5ff9b6-3784-5e77-821c-de7d598b9194" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79164/selection/bea3cff3908d84a722dff0c81360fee974679b7fccb41314b87ff01125047d86" :answer/id #uuid "2793ba80-2aef-597e-84e9-e9b5672c014d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79164/selection/591b64639a279e0471beded7941a5370384021079af943467159b4f50ccf44dc" :answer/id #uuid "ea926645-60a4-5152-bf9c-a62be6a71557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\