heta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038487/assets/6f27674dd7382f9040cdeb8e85ea35ff63e581ef5752b373aa0ab87a0b3e2f0f.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the required three-quarter-circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the three-quarter-circle are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79166/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d81c7ff-8459-5559-bfae-c2a9c3bc739e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79168/selection/3a0472f96eccaa2c8746fb82da346e062d6cd3ce394434f334ccfd0c4ee2173b" :answer/id #uuid "32676c82-5ca7-56cc-94f5-d84d3d35c7bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79168/selection/9c3ca3595ca5475694d3df88845530df43115acaa0f1a17324f72afe6f7481dd" :answer/id #uuid "a678dc53-3d82-5faf-a5ce-08ade66383a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{5\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79168/selection/bc3e76ff6c2251409d67bd4d44714df545c2e1406f35c243db21f791e2a3cb52" :answer/id #uuid "16d4ea9e-0021-5012-8ae3-12b0428a6559" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79168/selection/0291954faf78aee60aa7cb0a7430cbafea24e2d980b957a994a87dbe0a62ece4" :answer/id #uuid "65dbc84a-947b-5650-8306-f0dd3bd145cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{5\\pi }{4}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79168/selection/e770f8e6a3b3377282f44b76cd7a0728520f58d3e8c8d90bd3420eb08a0e46